            <div xml:id="d888">

                <pb facs="0843" n="837" xml:id="pg837"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">667.003/304: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-04-25T12:00:00+02:00">April 25,
                        1939—noon.</date><lb/>[Received 12:46 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>61. I learn that as from April 20 the Turkish tariff was made applicable to the
                    Hatay. This involves payment on imports into that area not only of Turkish
                    duties but also of Turkish consumption and transaction taxes and other
                    incidental taxes and minor charges.</p>
                <p>Inform Commerce.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Paris, Beirut.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
